<title>UK: UK's Halifax says house prices fell 0.6 pct in Jan.</title>
<headline>UK's Halifax says house prices fell 0.6 pct in Jan.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Halifax Building Society</p>
<p>released the following seasonally adjusted UK house price data -</p>
<p> HOUSE PRICES (index base 1983=100)    Jan	Dec	 Jan 96</p>
<p> Seasonally adjusted index		214.7    216.0     200.4</p>
<p> Monthly change (in pct)		   -0.6	1.1	 0.5</p>
<p> Annual change (in pct)		     7.1	8.4	-1.2</p>
<p>NOTE - The Halifax said house price inflation in the UK is expected to remain around 7.0 percent in 1997.</p>
<p>It said house prices normally show a fall in January, but the fall in January 1997 was sharper than expected and was probably an &quot;adjustment&quot; for larger than expected rises at the end of 1996.</p>
<p>It added that prices paid by first-time buyers fell by 2.0 percent in January and were now 5.7 percent higher than a year ago.</p>
<p>-- Kate Kelland, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7708</p>
</text>
